\ Bounded-memory regression for the library `connect` client path.
\
\ `connect` runs a Happy-Eyeballs race inside an internal task-scope that spawns
\ one connect-attempt task per resolved address, plus a connect-deadline task.
\
\ Every child is terminal before connect returns, yet before scope-exit reaping
\ each was retained in its home scheduler's finished_tasks until scheduler
\ teardown. A client calling connect in a loop therefore grew with the total
\ number of past connections. Scope-exit reaping now releases those children
\ when connect's internal scope exits, so a loop of connects stays bounded.
\
\ The server here is a minimal raw listen plus a spawned accept-loop that only
\ accepts and closes. The only tasks under test are the ones connect spawns
\ internally, so a failure isolates the client-side leak. This works cross-worker
\ as well as same-worker, so the `.flags` sidecar pins no thread count: connect's
\ children stay bounded wherever they land.
\
\ A regression that stops reaping connect's scope children retains every attempt
\ and deadline task and exhausts the 64 MB cap in the `.flags` sidecar partway
\ through the loop, dying with a memory-limit error instead of printing the
\ marker.
\
\ The iteration count is sized empirically: with scope-exit reaping disabled, the cap trips
\ between 75 and 150 iterations, so 250 fails reliably while running about 1.1 seconds
\ standalone against the 10-second harness cap. Each iteration pays cross-worker
\ cancel/await round trips on connect's deadline task, so this test degrades worse than
\ fair-share under full-suite load; the count buys the margin for that.
\
\ NOTE: This is a fixed-port socket test, so it carries some inherent flakiness
\       from port reuse and listen-before-connect timing. If it proves very flaky,
\       it can be temporarily disabled.

use "net" ;
use "net/tcp" ;
use "time" ;

[
  accept-loop: ( server -- ) [
    dup accept drop stream-close accept-loop
  ] ;

  "127.0.0.1" 39525 make-addr:tcp 128 listen
  dup [ accept-loop ] curry spawn

  100 milliseconds sleep

  250 [
    "127.0.0.1" 39525 make-addr:tcp connect
    stream-close
  ] times

  cancel-task
  close
] task-scope

"bounded" print-line
